---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import context from '../assets/eql/context.jpg';
import chaos from '../assets/eql/chaos.jpg';
import lx from '../assets/eql/lx.jpg';
import alexHead from '../assets/eql/alex-head.jpg';
import step1 from '../assets/eql/step1.jpg';
import step2 from '../assets/eql/step2.jpg';
import step3 from '../assets/eql/step3.jpg';
import step4 from '../assets/eql/step4.jpg';
import step5 from '../assets/eql/step5.jpg';

const toc = [
  ['where', 'Where EQL sits'],
  ['chaos', 'The cloud of chaos'],
  ['problem', 'The problem'],
  ['alex', 'Meet Alex'],
  ['lx', 'Mapping the launch'],
  ['fair', 'Fair from both sides'],
  ['questions', 'Open questions'],
];

const steps = [
  { img: step1, t: 'A great war with the bots', alt: 'CNBC article "Why bots make it so hard to buy Nikes", a sticky note and Reddit comments about botting',
    p: 'Alex is up against software, not other fans. CNBC’s piece “Why bots make it so hard to buy Nikes” sums it up, and one line stuck with me: the Nike SNKRS app gets 12 billion bot attempts a month. Fans in the comments say it plainly: you need a bot to get a hyped pair.' },
  { img: step2, t: 'Proving they’re human with inhumane UX', alt: 'reCAPTCHA checkbox and an image grid asking to select traffic lights',
    p: 'To get in, Alex has to prove their humanity by clicking traffic lights, and trains someone’s AI for free while doing it. The defence against bots is paid for with the fan’s patience.' },
  { img: step3, t: 'Waiting in agony', alt: 'A queue screen saying 2000+ people ahead of you',
    p: '“You are now in the queue. 2000+ people ahead of you.” A progress bar that barely moves, with no sense of whether there’s anything left at the end of it.' },
  { img: step4, t: 'Watching the empire crash when it matters most', alt: 'News of Stanley cup chaos at Target and a Ticketek error page with an apology',
    p: 'When the moment arrives, the site goes down. Stanley cups selling out in minutes at Target, Ticketek apologising for “a problem processing your request”. The brand loses trust at its biggest moment.' },
  { img: step5, t: 'Seeing vultures resell for 5x more', alt: 'StockX logo',
    p: 'Then the product Alex wanted shows up on resale marketplaces like StockX for five times the price. The fan loses, and so does the brand that wanted that fan to own it.' },
];
---
<Base title="My research on EQL · Talal Athar" description="Talal’s research on launch experiences: where EQL sits, the cloud of chaos, and one fan’s journey through a hyped drop.">
  <div class="rx-progress" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
  <article class="rx">
    <header class="rx-head">
      <a class="rx-back" href="/">← Back to homepage</a>
      <p class="rx-kicker"><span class="eql-logo">EQL</span> Research · written for the EQL team</p>
      <h1>Making every launch <span class="hl">chaotic good</span></h1>
      <p class="rx-lede">I’m applying to EQL, so before talking to the team I wanted to understand the problem from the outside in. This is my working research: where EQL sits, what goes wrong during a hyped product drop, and one fan’s journey through it. It’s a starting point for a conversation, not a conclusion.</p>
      <nav class="rx-anchors" aria-label="On this page">
        {toc.map(([id, label]) => <a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a>)}
      </nav>
    </header>

    <div class="rx-grid">
      <aside class="rx-toc" aria-label="Contents">
        <p>Contents</p>
        <ol>{toc.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`} data-toc={id}>{label}</a></li>)}</ol>
      </aside>

      <div class="rx-body">
        <section id="where">
          <h2><span class="n">01</span>Where EQL sits</h2>
          <p>EQL sits at the intersection of pop culture and commerce. When the two collide, you get a cultural moment that people want to own a piece of.</p>
          <div class="rx-eq" aria-label="Project Hail Mary plus Nike equals Nike x PHM sneakers">
            <span class="pill culture">Project Hail Mary <small>culture</small></span>
            <span class="op">+</span>
            <span class="pill commerce">Nike <small>commerce</small></span>
            <span class="op">=</span>
            <span class="pill result">Nike × PHM sneakers</span>
          </div>
          <p>This is a moment in our culture. Retailers and brands will try to capture it. Fans will try to own the product. EQL’s job is to make sure the moment goes to the right people.</p>
          <figure class="rx-fig rx-fig--narrow">
            <Image src={context} alt="Diagram of EQL at the intersection of pop culture and commerce, with a Nike x Project Hail Mary sneaker as the example" widths={[520, 1040]} sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 520px" />
            <figcaption>My sketch of EQL’s position, with a hypothetical collab as the example.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </section>

        <section id="chaos">
          <h2><span class="n">02</span>The cloud of chaos</h2>
          <p>A cloud of chaos covers the launch experience (LX) of in-demand, hot products. It creates bad UX for fans and for retailers alike. Traditional ecommerce platforms crumble under these cultural moments, because they weren’t built for this kind of chaos.</p>
          <ul class="rx-forces">
            <li><b>🕵️</b><span>Hackers and scammers trying to game the system</span></li>
            <li><b>🤖</b><span>Attacks by bots</span></li>
            <li><b>🌊</b><span>Heavy traffic all at once</span></li>
            <li><b>🔥</b><span>Sites crashing</span></li>
          </ul>
          <figure class="rx-fig rx-fig--narrow">
            <Image src={chaos} alt="Sketch of a chaos cloud raining down on the launch experience, branching into hackers, bots, traffic and crashing sites" widths={[520, 1040]} sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 520px" />
            <figcaption>The cloud of chaos sits on top of the launch experience.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </section>

        <section id="problem" class="rx-problem">
          <p class="rx-label">Problem statement</p>
          <p class="rx-hmw">How might we make a product launch experience <span class="hl">chaos‑free</span> (or chaotic good) for both fans and retailers?</p>
        </section>

        <section id="alex">
          <h2><span class="n">03</span>Meet Alex</h2>
          <p>To make this concrete, I followed one fan. Alex is really passionate about collectibles: retro music tech, trading cards, action figures. Here’s what a hyped launch looks like from Alex’s side.</p>
          <figure class="rx-fig">
            <Image src={alexHead} alt="Alex (fan) is really passionate about collectibles: retro music tech, cards and action figures" widths={[680, 1360]} sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" />
          </figure>
          <ol class="rx-steps">
            {steps.map((s, i) => (
              <li>
                <span class="rx-dot">{i + 1}</span>
                <div>
                  <h3>{s.t}</h3>
                  <p>{s.p}</p>
                  <figure class="rx-fig rx-fig--step">
                    <Image src={s.img} alt={s.alt} widths={[420, 840]} sizes="420px" />
                  </figure>
                </div>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
          <p class="rx-aside">Every step is a moment where the brand had Alex’s full attention, and spent it on friction.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="lx">
          <h2><span class="n">04</span>Mapping the launch experience</h2>
          <p>I split the launch experience into three journeys. Each one is a chance to replace chaos with something fans and retailers can trust.</p>
          <div class="rx-phases">
            <div><p class="ph">1 · Before launch</p><ul><li>Hype and buzz</li><li>“Notify me” as a pulse check on demand</li></ul></div>
            <div><p class="ph">2 · During launch</p><ul><li>Real-time insights</li><li>What sizes people want</li><li>Who they are (demographics)</li></ul></div>
            <div><p class="ph">3 · After launch</p><ul><li>How you reach out to winners</li><li>How you reach those who missed out (for example with an EQL score)</li></ul></div>
          </div>
          <figure class="rx-fig">
            <Image src={lx} alt="Mind map of the launch experience split into before, during and post launch journeys" widths={[680, 1360, 2000]} sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" />
            <figcaption>My map of the launch experience, from the FigJam board.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </section>

        <section id="fair">
          <h2><span class="n">05</span>Fair from both sides</h2>
          <p>A fair launch has two halves: rules that keep the draw honest, and knowing who your real fans are.</p>
          <div class="rx-stickies">
            <div class="rx-sticky" style="--r:-2deg"><b>Run it fair</b><ul><li>Only humans can enter (sorry, bots)</li><li>One entry per person</li><li>A raffle system</li></ul></div>
            <div class="rx-sticky" style="--r:2deg"><b>Know the fans</b><ul><li>Verified fans</li><li>Loyal, repeat fans</li><li>Bad eggs</li></ul></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="questions">
          <h2><span class="n">06</span>Open questions I’d bring to the team</h2>
          <p>These came up while mapping and I don’t have answers yet. They’re what I’d want to dig into first.</p>
          <ul class="rx-qs">
            <li><b>Raffle or first come, first served?</b> When does each one feel fair to fans, and when does it suit the retailer?</li>
            <li><b>Plugging into the order management system (OMS).</b> How does a fair draw hand off cleanly to a retailer’s existing order flow?</li>
            <li><b>The fans who miss out.</b> Most entrants don’t win. How do we talk to them so they come back to the next drop instead of the resale market?</li>
            <li><b>“Notify me” as a signal.</b> Can the before-launch moment tell retailers what sizes and quantities to expect?</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <footer class="rx-end">
          <p>Thanks for reading. I’d love to talk about where this goes next.</p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn" href="/contact">Reach out</a>
            <a class="btn btn--light" href="/#work">See my case studies</a>
          </div>
        </footer>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <script>
    const bar = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.rx-progress span');
    const onScroll = () => {
      const h = document.documentElement;
      const p = h.scrollTop / Math.max(1, h.scrollHeight - h.clientHeight);
      if (bar) bar.style.transform = `scaleX(${p})`;
    };
    addEventListener('scroll', onScroll, { passive: true }); onScroll();
    const links = new Map([...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('[data-toc]')].map((a) => [a.dataset.toc, a]));
    const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
      for (const e of entries) if (e.isIntersecting) {
        links.forEach((a) => a.removeAttribute('aria-current'));
        links.get(e.target.id)?.setAttribute('aria-current', 'true');
      }
    }, { rootMargin: '-30% 0px -60% 0px' });
    links.forEach((_, id) => { const s = document.getElementById(id!); if (s) io.observe(s); });
  </script>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  .rx-progress { position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 3px; z-index: 60; pointer-events: none; }
  .rx-progress span { display: block; height: 100%; background: #ffd400; transform-origin: 0 50%; transform: scaleX(0); }
  .rx { --rx-ink: #0a0a0a; --rx-muted: #5c5c5c; color: var(--rx-ink); background: #fafaf7; border: 1.5px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 rgba(29,27,58,.9); padding: clamp(24px, 5vw, 64px) clamp(18px, 4vw, 56px); margin: 0 auto 48px; max-width: 1100px; }
  .rx .hl { background: #ffd400; padding: 0 .12em; border-radius: .12em; box-decoration-break: clone; -webkit-box-decoration-break: clone; }
  .rx-back { font-size: 14px; color: var(--rx-muted); text-decoration: none; }
  .rx-back:hover { color: var(--rx-ink); }
  .rx-kicker { margin: 28px 0 10px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; color: var(--rx-muted); }
  .rx-head h1 { font-size: clamp(40px, 7vw, 84px); line-height: 1.06; letter-spacing: -.035em; font-weight: 900; margin: 0 0 20px; max-width: 14ch; text-wrap: balance; }
  .rx-lede { font-size: clamp(18px, 2vw, 21px); line-height: 1.55; max-width: 60ch; margin: 0 0 24px; color: #2b2b2b; }
  .rx-anchors { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; padding-bottom: 28px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e3e3dc; }
  .rx-anchors a { font-size: 14px; padding: 6px 12px; border: 1px solid #d6d6cf; border-radius: 999px; text-decoration: none; color: var(--rx-ink); background: #fff; }
  .rx-anchors a:hover { background: var(--rx-ink); color: #fff; }
  .rx-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 190px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 56px; margin-top: 48px; }
  .rx-toc { position: sticky; top: 64px; align-self: start; font-size: 14px; }
  .rx-toc p { margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--rx-muted); }
  .rx-toc ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 2px; border-left: 2px solid #e3e3dc; }
  .rx-toc a { display: block; padding: 5px 12px; margin-left: -2px; border-left: 2px solid transparent; color: var(--rx-muted); text-decoration: none; }
  .rx-toc a:hover { color: var(--rx-ink); }
  .rx-toc a[aria-current] { color: var(--rx-ink); font-weight: 700; border-left-color: #ffd400; }
  .rx-body { max-width: 680px; }
  .rx-body section { scroll-margin-top: 64px; margin: 0 0 80px; }
  .rx-body h2 { font-size: clamp(28px, 3.6vw, 40px); letter-spacing: -.025em; line-height: 1.08; font-weight: 800; margin: 0 0 16px; text-wrap: balance; }
  .rx-body h2 .n { display: block; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .12em; color: var(--rx-muted); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .rx-body p { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .rx-fig { margin: 28px 0; }
  .rx-fig img { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 14px; border: 1px solid #e0e0d8; background: #fff; }
  .rx-fig--narrow { max-width: 520px; }
  .rx-fig--step { max-width: 420px; margin: 14px 0 0; }
  .rx-fig figcaption { font-size: 14px; color: var(--rx-muted); margin-top: 8px; }
  .rx-eq { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin: 24px 0; }
  .rx-eq .pill { display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; padding: 10px 16px; border-radius: 14px; border: 1.5px solid var(--rx-ink); background: #fff; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.2; }
  .rx-eq small { font-weight: 600; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .rx-eq .culture small { color: #c026d3; }
  .rx-eq .commerce small { color: #7c3aed; }
  .rx-eq .result { background: #ffd400; }
  .rx-eq .op { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 800; }
  .rx-forces { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 24px 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 10px; }
  .rx-forces li { display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: center; background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e0e0d8; border-radius: 14px; padding: 14px 16px; font-weight: 600; }
  .rx-forces b { font-size: 24px; }
  .rx-problem { background: var(--rx-ink); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 40px); }
  .rx-label { font-size: 12px !important; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #ffd400; margin: 0 0 10px !important; }
  .rx-hmw { font-size: clamp(24px, 3.2vw, 34px) !important; line-height: 1.2 !important; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: 0 !important; }
  .rx-hmw .hl { color: var(--rx-ink); }
  .rx-steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 32px 0; position: relative; }
  .rx-steps::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 17px; top: 8px; bottom: 8px; width: 2px; background: repeating-linear-gradient(#0a0a0a 0 6px, transparent 6px 12px); }
  .rx-steps li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 36px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 40px; position: relative; }
  .rx-dot { width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 50%; background: #ffd400; border: 2px solid var(--rx-ink); display: grid; place-items: center; font-weight: 900; }
  .rx-steps h3 { font-size: 21px; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 4px 0 8px; }
  .rx-aside { font-style: italic; color: var(--rx-muted); border-left: 3px solid #ffd400; padding-left: 14px; }
  .rx-phases { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 12px; margin: 24px 0; }
  .rx-phases > div { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e0e0d8; border-radius: 14px; padding: 16px; min-width: 0; }
  .rx-phases .ph { font-size: 13px !important; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 0 0 8px !important; }
  .rx-phases ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .rx-stickies { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin: 28px 0; }
  .rx-sticky { background: #ff9fd6; padding: 20px 22px 26px; rotate: var(--r); box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.12); font-family: 'Marker Felt', 'Comic Sans MS', var(--sans); }
  .rx-sticky b { font-size: 20px; }
  .rx-sticky ul { margin: 10px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .rx-qs { padding: 0; list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 12px; margin: 20px 0; }
  .rx-qs li { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e0e0d8; border-radius: 14px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .rx-qs b { display: block; }
  .rx-end { border-top: 1px solid #e3e3dc; padding-top: 32px; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .rx-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; }
    .rx-toc { display: none; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .rx-forces, .rx-phases, .rx-stickies { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .rx-body p { font-size: 17px; }
  }
</style>
